@startuml
title SRM Quotation Lifecycle - State Machine
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #334155
  ArrowColor #475569
}

[*] --> Draft : Supplier starts response
Draft --> Submitted : Submit before deadline
Draft --> Withdrawn : Supplier withdraws draft
Submitted --> ValidationFailed : Mandatory data invalid
ValidationFailed --> Draft : Supplier corrects response
before deadline
Submitted --> TechnicallyUnderReview : Technical evaluation required
Submitted --> CommerciallyUnderReview : Technical review not configured
TechnicallyUnderReview --> ClarificationRequired : Clarification requested
ClarificationRequired --> TechnicallyUnderReview : Supplier responds
TechnicallyUnderReview --> TechnicallyAccepted : Technical requirements pass
TechnicallyUnderReview --> TechnicallyRejected : Technical requirements fail
TechnicallyAccepted --> CommerciallyUnderReview : Commercial evaluation starts
CommerciallyUnderReview --> UnderNegotiation : Negotiation initiated
CommerciallyUnderReview --> Finalized : No negotiation required
UnderNegotiation --> UnderNegotiation : New negotiation round/version
UnderNegotiation --> Finalized : Final terms confirmed
Finalized --> Awarded : RFQ award recorded for supplier
Finalized --> Unsuccessful : Another supplier is awarded
Submitted --> Disqualified : Authorized disqualification
with reason
TechnicallyRejected --> Unsuccessful : Evaluation completed
Withdrawn --> [*]
TechnicallyRejected --> [*]
Disqualified --> [*]
Awarded --> [*]
Unsuccessful --> [*]

note right of Submitted
A submitted quotation is immutable.
Any permitted revision creates a new
version with actor, timestamp and history.
No supplier can view competing quotations.
end note

note bottom of CommerciallyUnderReview
Comparison basis (for example landed cost),
ranking and evaluation criteria are configurable.
end note
@enduml
